  "name": "linalg",
  "description": "A pedagogical linear algebra library implemented in early-stage Rust, providing fundamental matrix structures and linear system operations. It features a generic two-dimensional matrix implementation with support for row and column iteration, matrix augmentation, and row-wise manipulations. The project serves as a functional exploration of matrix calculus and linear equation substitution using Rust's primitive type system.",
